    "title": "Hornets vs. Celtics: Free Live Stream, TV Channel, How to Watch - Bleacher Nation",
    "text": "The Charlotte Hornets (39-35) square off against the Boston Celtics (49-24) at 6 p.m. ET on Sunday, March 29, 2026 on NBCS-BOS and FDSSE. The Hornets dropped their most recent game 118-114 against the 76ers on Saturday. The Celtics enter this contest following a 109-102 victory over the Hawks on Friday. In the Hornets’ loss, Brandon Miller led the way with a team-high 29 points (adding eight rebounds and zero assists). Payton Pritchard scored a team-high 36 points for the Celtics in the victory. When is Hornets vs. Celtics? This contest between the Hornets and Celtics will go down on Sunday, March 29, 2026. Expect to see the opening tip at 6 p.m. ET. Where to watch Hornets vs. Celtics The Hornets and Celtics will hit the floor at Spectrum Center for this matchup on March 29, and if you would like to catch the action live, get your tickets now from Vivid Seats! What channel is the game on? You can catch this game live on NBCS-BOS, FDSSE. Hornets vs. Celtics Game Preview Hornets Stats, Odds & Insights This season, the Hornets have been favored 29 times and won 23, or 79.3%, of those games. The 116.3 points per game the Hornets record are 9.4 more points than the Celtics give up (106.9 points per game). The Hornets knock down 16.4 three-pointers per game (first in the league) at a 38.1% rate (third-best in the NBA), compared to the 12.8 per game their opponents make at a 35.9% rate. The Hornets’ offense has been much worse in home games (115.2 PPG) compared to away games (117.4 PPG). However, their defense has been better when playing at home (111.1 PPG allowed) when compared to road games (112.4 PPG allowed). The Hornets have seen an uptick in scoring recently, racking up 117.3 points per game in their last 10 outings, 1.0 point more than the 116.3 they’ve scored this year. Celtics Stats, Odds & Insights The Celtics outscore opponents by 7.2 points per game (posting 114.1 points per game, 20th in league, and giving up 106.9 per outing, first in NBA) and have a +526 scoring differential. The Celtics put up an average of 114.1 points per game. That’s only 2.4 more points than the 111.7 the Hornets allow. The Celtics are the third-best team in the league in 3-pointers made (15.2 per game) and 11th in 3-point percentage (36.1%). The Celtics score the same amount of points per game at home as away (114.1), and concede more at home (107.0) than on the road (106.9). The Celtics are averaging 111.5 points per game in their past 10 games, which is 2.6 fewer points than their average for the season (114.1). Hornets Key Players to Watch Hornets Leaders Name GP PTS REB ASST STL BLK 3PM Brandon Miller 57 20.5 5.1 3.4 1.0 0.7 3.2 LaMelo Ball 64 19.7 4.8 7.1 1.2 0.2 3.7 Kon Knueppel 73 19.0 5.4 3.5 0.7 0.2 3.5 Coby White 43 17.8 3.6 4.3 0.6 0.1 2.3 Miles Bridges 69 17.1 5.9 3.2 0.6 0.4 1.9 Celtics Key Players to Watch Celtics Leaders Name GP PTS REB ASST STL BLK 3PM Jaylen Brown 65 28.6 7.0 5.2 1.0 0.4 1.9 Jayson Tatum 10 19.8 9.5 3.8 1.2 0.1 2.7 Derrick White 70 17.1 4.5 5.5 1.2 1.4 2.8 Payton Pritchard 71 16.9 4.0 5.2 0.7 0.1 2.6 Neemias Queta 69 9.8 8.3 1.6 0.8 1.3 0.0 Read more NBA Game previews as well as view the latest live NBA lines on Betsperts. Get the latest NBA picks and predictions as well as the daily top NBA Player Prop Bets to choose from. Or, if you are new to sports betting, read our in-depth guide on how to bet on basketball as well as find the best NBA betting sites.",
